From: Jetha Chan <jetha@splatterfacegames.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: helpers: leave slack after the NV12 chroma plane

On MSM8953 (Venus firmware VIDEO.VE.4.2-00078) the encoder never consumed
an input buffer unless the frame was 640x480. With firmware debug messages
enabled every EmptyThisBuffer was refused:

  venc_EmptyThisBuffer(7152): ETB offset size 0[--expected is less than -128]
  or allocLen 1413120 [expected is greater than 1413248]

that is, the firmware requires the buffer to extend at least 128 bytes
past the NV12 planes. get_framesize_raw_nv12() returns the two planes
rounded up to 4K, which is exact whenever the plane sizes are multiples
of 4K: 1280x736 (1280x720 aligned), 1920x1088 and 512x640 all came out
exact and failed; 640x480 has 2K of rounding slack in the chroma plane
and worked. The input queue then stalls without an error, and V4L2
clients (v4l2-ctl, ffmpeg h264_v4l2m2m) wait forever.

Add 4K after the chroma plane before rounding. The same size is used for
decoder capture buffers, which only grow by 4K.

Tested on MSM8953 (Lenovo ThinkSmart View) with v4l2-ctl: H.264 encode
now runs at 640x480, 1280x720, 1920x1080, 490x652, 980x1304 and 1304x980
(30 frames each, valid streams of the requested size), and 60 camera
frames each at 490x652 and 980x1304 (1.0 s and 2.0 s).

Signed-off-by: Jetha Chan <jetha@splatterfacegames.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
index 7c094009c..cf3a4668f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
@@ -955,7 +955,12 @@ static u32 get_framesize_raw_nv12(u32 width, u32 height)
 
 	y_plane = y_stride * y_sclines;
 	uv_plane = uv_stride * uv_sclines;
-	size = y_plane + uv_plane;
+	/*
+	 * The firmware rejects an input buffer that does not extend at least
+	 * 128 bytes past the end of the chroma plane, so never let the 4K
+	 * rounding come out exact.
+	 */
+	size = y_plane + uv_plane + SZ_4K;
 
 	return ALIGN(size, SZ_4K);
 }
